{"timestamp":"2026-10-02T10:43:29.388Z","ordinal":74,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0fc35-6f78-7e40-a9f7-24a43aec4a76","turn_id":"01a0fc35-6fc9-7241-b56b-0815803451df","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2418fc27-ee31-47d3-8c4a-72b5fb447175","process_id":"69510","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat src/lib/archiveChunks.js; sed -n '1,260p' Cloud/scripts/restore.mjs; cat scripts/lib/stream-manifest.mjs"],"cwd":"file:///Users/zenray/Create/Build/Productions/GithubProductions/ZenRayProgress","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat src/lib/archiveChunks.js","name":"archiveChunks.js","path":"src/lib/archiveChunks.js"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,260p' Cloud/scripts/restore.mjs","name":"restore.mjs","path":"Cloud/scripts/restore.mjs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat scripts/lib/stream-manifest.mjs","name":"stream-manifest.mjs","path":"scripts/lib/stream-manifest.mjs"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"// archiveChunks.js — PURE resolution of archive manifests .file.json (v2 / v3 / v4 multi-shard).\n//\n// Plainly: an archived file is NOT stored whole on GitHub. It is cut into 19 MB \"chunks\" spread\n// over one or more repos (shards). The .file.json manifest is the map: it says where the chunks\n// are and in what order to re-glue them. This file centralizes that map reading, which used to be\n// COPY-PASTED across 3 components (FileNodeViewer, DownloadsView, QuickLookOverlay) — with\n// divergences (QuickLook ignored parts[] -> broken on big v4 multi-shard files). One source now.\n//\n// PURITY: no network logic here (no fetch, no Blob). Just: from a manifest, produce the ORDERED\n// list of raw URLs to fetch, and pick the right version. Actual downloading lives in fetchAsset.js\n// (which consumes these URLs). ABSOLUTE backward compat: existing v2/v3/v4 manifests (130 GB)\n// resolve exactly as before — this module REPRODUCES FileNodeViewer's behavior, never changes it.\n\nexport const OWNER = 'mat